	(text "Command word = the last 16 bits clocked into MOSI before LATCH rises (MSB first):\n  bit 0  -> SKB 38 FRONT PANEL LOCKOUT      bit 7  -> SKB 45 INTEGRATION TIME (2)\n  bit 1  -> SKB 39 SAMPLE (contact to 0 V)   bit 8  -> SKB 46 INTEGRATION TIME (1)\n  bit 2  -> SKB 40 SAMPLE pulse (via Q1)     bit 9  -> SKB 47 AUTORANGE command\n  bit 3  -> SKB 41 RATIO                     bit 10 -> SKB 48 RANGE (1)\n  bit 4  -> SKB 42 FUNCTION                  bit 11 -> SKB 49 RANGE (2)\n  bit 5  -> SKB 43 FUNCTION                  bit 12 -> SKB 50 RANGE (4)\n  bit 6  -> SKB 44 INTEGRATION TIME (4)      bit 13..15 spare\n\nA 1 turns the open-drain output ON, i.e. pulls the SKB line to logic 0\n(bit 2: a 1 drives SKB 40 HIGH through Q1).  The multimeter has its own\n4.7k pull-ups to +5 V on every command line.\n\n~{G} (OEn_ISO) is pulled high until the MCU enables it, and all drains are\noff without isolated power, so an unpowered / unconfigured board leaves\nthe multimeter exactly as if nothing were plugged in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150 84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dbe98e29-797f-5e3b-ac29-5676559c72eb")
	)
